1. STAR CITIZEN GAME TEXT

   Gloss reads the game's English localisation table out of the user's own
   Data.p4k, and writes a copy of it back with a handful of names annotated.
   That text is Cloud Imperium's, both before and after Gloss touches it.

   None of it is in this repository, and no release published from it contains
   any: the releases carry the tool and a table of derived facts, and the
   annotated file is produced on the user's own machine from their own
   installation. If you fork this and choose to distribute a built global.ini
   instead, that is redistribution of Cloud Imperium's text, and it is on you -
   nothing in LICENSE grants you a right to it, and this project cannot grant
   one.

2. THE ACQUISITION FACTS

   facts.json is derived from the Star Citizen Wiki API, which in turn derives
   from Cloud Imperium's game data and, for prices, from UEX's crowd-sourced
   listings. It is published here as a convenience so that nobody has to make
   12,000 requests to build it themselves. See CREDITS.md.

3. STARSTRINGS

